  "chapter": {
    "number": 9,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "For the end, a Psalm of David, concerning the secrets of the Son."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will give thanks to you, O Lord, with my whole heart; I will recount all your wonderful works.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will be glad and exult in you: I will sing to your name, O you Most High.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When my enemies are turned back, they shall be feeble and perish at your presence.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you have maintained my cause and my right; you sat on the throne, that judge righteousness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have rebuked the nations, and the ungodly one has perished; you have blotted out their name for ever, even for ever and ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The swords of the enemy have failed utterly; and you have destroyed cities: their memorial has been destroyed with a noise,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "but the Lord endures for ever: he has prepared his throne for judgment.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he will judge the world in righteousness, he will judge the nations in uprightness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord also is become a refuge for the poor, a seasonable help, in affliction.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And let them that know your name hope in you: for you, O Lord, have not failed them that diligently seek you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Sing praises to the Lord, who dwells in Sion: declare his dealings among the nations.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he remembered them, in making inquisition for blood: he has not forgotten the supplication of the poor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Have mercy upon me, O Lord; look upon my affliction which I suffer of my enemies, you that lift me up from the gates of death:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "that I may declare all your praises in the gates of the daughter of Sion: I will exult in your salvation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The heathen are caught in the destruction which they planned: in the very snare which they hid is their foot taken.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is known as executing judgments: the sinner is taken in the works of his hands. A song of Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let sinners be driven away into Hades, even all the nations that forget God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the poor shall not be forgotten for ever: the patience of the needy ones shall not perish for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Arise, O Lord, let not man prevail: let the heathen be judged before you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Appoint, O Lord, a lawgiver over them: let the heathen know that they are men. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          },
          {
            "text": "(Psalm 9a",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 16
          },
          {
            "text": ")",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Why stand you afar off, O Lord? why do you overlook us in times of need, in affliction?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "While the ungodly one acts proudly, the poor is",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 17
          },
          {
            "text": "hotly pursued: the wicked are taken in the crafty counsels which they imagine.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Because the sinner praises himself for the desires of his heart; and the unjust one blesses himself.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The sinner has provoked the Lord: according to the abundance of his",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 18
          },
          {
            "text": "pride he will not seek after him: God is not before him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 25,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "His ways are",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 19
          },
          {
            "text": "profane at all times; your judgments are removed from before him: he will gain the mastery over all his enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 26,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he has said in his heart, I shall not be moved, continuing without evil from generation to generation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 27,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Whose mouth is full of cursing, and bitterness, and fraud: under his tongue are trouble and pain.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 28,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He lies in wait with rich men in secret places, in order to kill the innocent: his eyes are",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 20
          },
          {
            "text": "set against the poor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 29,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He lies in wait in secret as a lion in his den: he lies in wait to ravish the poor, to ravish the poor when he draws him after him: he will bring him down in his snare.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 30,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He will bow down and fall when he has mastered the poor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 31,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he has said in his heart, God has forgotten: he has turned away his face so as never to look.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 32,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Arise, O Lord God; let your hand be lifted up: forget not the poor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 33,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore, has the wicked provoked God? for he has said in his heart, He will not require it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 34,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You see it; for you do observe trouble and wrath, to deliver them into your hands: the poor has been left to you; you were a helper to the orphan.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 35,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Break you the arm of the sinner and wicked man: his sin shall be sought for, and shall not be found.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 36,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord shall reign for ever, even for ever and ever: you⌃ Gentiles shall perish out his land.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 37,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord has heard the desire of the poor: your ear has inclined to the preparation of their heart;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 38,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "to plead for the orphan and afflicted, that man may no more boast upon the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 16,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Note. - Here begins a change of numbers as compared with the Heb. which continues to Ps. 146, this psalm having no number, and the eleventh being called the tenth. The following verses 21-37 are numbered 1-18 in the original text.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 9,
          "verse": 20
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 17,
